  "summary": "于先生二十七岁入日本商社，语言能力与工业市场需求使其早得财。命身未空宫借丑武贪，酉火星同禄存左辅与丑贪狼组成作者所谓火贪吉格。癸巳限事业酉宫廉破禄存同宫，破军化禄吉化事业及命宫，贪狼化忌与火星制煞为用，被作者解释为重机械业务的辛劳而非必凶。末句未完不补。",
  "summary_en": "Mr. Yu joined a Japanese trading company at twenty-seven; language skills and demand for industrial machinery supported early prosperity. His empty Life and Body Palaces at Wei borrow Wu Qu–Tan Lang influence from Chou. Huo Xing with Lu Cun and Zuo Fu at You combines with Tan Lang at Chou in the author’s favorable Huo Tan configuration. In the Gui Si cycle, Lian Zhen, Po Jun and Lu Cun share the You Career Palace; Po Jun Hua Lu strengthens Career and Life. Huo Xing and Tan Lang Hua Ji are put to use, interpreted as demanding heavy-machinery work rather than inevitable harm. The final unfinished qualification is not completed.",
